ood she accidentally  smeared across her face following her  parents murders the staff she wields  incorporates her father's last gift to  her and one of her bracelets is the  first thing she successfully stole based  on her calling card which can be  discovered in the train yard vault on  world's edge  she's leaned into the Portuguese  translation of her name and adopted a  wolf-like persona but what about her a  Bailey  well here's where the guesswork comes in  in describing lova respawn rates stylish  sophisticated and resourceful whatever  Lobo wants she takes good luck stopping  her this could imply a more aggressive  play style that has to do with securing  or stealing loot  so maybe Lobo is an offense or support  character let's run with that assumption  when trying to figure out her abilities  respawn seems to just love hinting at  upcoming content by Twitter or  cinematics prior to making an official  announcement for example we saw crypto  surveillance drone and drone EMP in the  forever family trailer we also saw  revenants stalker and deaf totem in the  season 4 launch trailer and silence in a  tweet from the apex legends Twitter  account so let's look at how the  developer has portrayed and teased Lobo  in the legacy of a thief's trailer we  see Lobo utilize a staff to both achieve  greater height while jumping and as a  melee weapon she also utilizes a piece  of tech that allows her to seemingly  teleport and of course as a thief we see  her steal like a lot pretty much  everything that hasn't been nailed down  of those three things only one has been  corroborated somewhere else Lobo has  actually already appeared in game she  can briefly show up on the lobby screen  where she playfully looks at you and  flips her hair and then teleports away  you can also find one of her bracelets  in the same vault where her calling card  is located interacting with it teleports  you to the location depicted on the  lobby screen which according to the  mini-map is on